[
  {
    "text": "I concede that the baseline no-show is established under POL-NS-01: the trip record EV-TRIP-00207 shows a driver 'arrived' event at 06:41:20 and termination by the driver at 06:49:37 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, and the GPS trace EV-GPS-00207 shows a continuous in-geofence run of 507 seconds from 06:41:10 to 06:49:37, exceeding the 300-second STANDARD minimum dwell, with the driver's minimum distance to the pin at 14.47 m, inside the 50 m arrival radius. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 are satisfied on this record.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00207", "EV-GPS-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
    "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "I concede that the rider's own presence and contact case fails: the rider's GPS track in EV-GPS-00207 places the device a minimum of 1,894 m from the pickup pin for the whole window, with 0 qualifying fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, and the chat log EV-CHAT-00207 contains four messages, all from SYSTEM or DRIVER, with the rider sending none. POL-NS-04 therefore does not apply: limb (a) fails because the rider sent no locating or coordinating message, and limb (c) is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes. The rider's assertion that he 'came down' is not supported by the record.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-CHAT-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
    "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "None of the rider-exonerating clauses displaces POL-NS-01. POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside the 50 m arrival radius (minimum distance 14.47 m), not outside it within 400 m. POL-NS-05 does not apply because at the 06:41:20 arrival marker the driver was inside the radius and not more than 300 m away or travelling at 15 kph or above. POL-NS-06 does not apply because the effective in-geofence dwell is 507 s, far longer than the 300 s STANDARD minimum, so there is no waiting-period shortfall.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-06"],
    "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The only traffic_advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00207-01, is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT covers Woodlands Ave 6 in this window. POL-NS-06 limb (i) is therefore unavailable to accumulate separate in-geofence intervals. This absence does not assist the rider, because the single continuous dwell of 507 s already exceeds the 300 s minimum and no shortfall exists for limb (i) to excuse.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00207-01", "EV-GPS-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
    "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec"
  },
  {
    "text": "The driver's profile EV-DPROF-00207 shows driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d = 7 and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d = 61. Seven is 4 or more, and 7 divided by 61 is approximately 0.115, which is greater than 0.08. Both limbs of the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check are therefore met. Under POL-NS-07, driver compensation is WITHHELD and the case must escalate under POL-NS-09; the escalation packet must DIRECT THE REVIEWER to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full, and the fee is held meanwhile rather than collected or refunded by the automated pipeline.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
    "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider's profile EV-RPROF-00207 shows rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d = 1, which is below the 3-or-more threshold in POL-NS-09(d), so that limb does not trip. However, POL-NS-09(d) is also triggered where the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check trips, which it does here; escalation is therefore required under POL-NS-09(d) on the anti-farming limb alone.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
    "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "Under POL-GEN-01, only driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d may be cited for the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test, and only rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d for POL-NS-09(d). The driver's prior_no_show_flags (0) is a lifetime counter and is not the trailing-30-day figure, and no other profile field—rating, cancellation_rate, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld, acceptance_rate, active_region—may ground this finding. I rely solely on the permitted fields.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207", "EV-RPROF-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-07"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The lawful outcome is ESCALATE, not NO_ACTION and not DRIVER_COMPENSATION. Under POL-GEN-03, ESCALATE is terminal: the Judge issues no monetary ruling, states the POL-NS-09(d) trigger and the open question, records the POL-NS-07 instruction into the packet, and the disputed SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded while review is pending. The fare breakdown EV-FARE-00207 already shows payment_status PENDING and refund_issued_sgd 0.0, so the rider is not carrying a collected charge; the packet must direct the reviewer to refund the SGD 4.00 in full, which is the rider's win on this record.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207", "EV-DPROF-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-07"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The contested amount is the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, which matches fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee of SGD 4.00 in EV-FARE-00207; the SGD 0.50 platform fee is not part of the no-show refund. The fee_schedule resolution_rule produces SGD 4.00 as the greater of the STANDARD zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so fare_breakdown is not impaired under POL-NS-08(d) and the refund instruction covers the correct SGD 4.00 line.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  }
]

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace places the driver 14.47 m from the pickup pin — inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius — with the first qualifying fix (accuracy 25 m or better) at 06:41:10, ten seconds before the trip_record 'arrived' event at 06:41:20. The driver was therefore inside the geofence at or before the arrival marker, satisfying POL-NS-01(b) and the three-consecutive-qualifying-fix test in POL-NS-02.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The longest continuous run of qualifying in-geofence fixes lasted 507 seconds, from 06:41:10 to 06:49:37, with no sampling gap (max_gap_sec 0, coverage 100%). That exceeds the 300-second minimum dwell for a STANDARD zone, measured from the first qualifying fix as POL-NS-01(c) requires, so the dwell condition is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record shows no boarding event (started_at and ended_at are null) and termination by the driver at 06:49:37 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, a recognised code. The required 300-second dwell elapsed at 06:46:10, so the cancellation at 06:49:37 was at or after that moment, satisfying POL-NS-01(d).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own GPS track shows the device never came within 1.9 km of the pin — minimum distance 1,894 m, mean 1,900 m, and zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius — and the chat log contains no message from the rider at all. The rider therefore sent no locating or coordinating message (POL-NS-04(a) fails) and was affirmatively not within the presence radius on admissible fixes (limb (c) failed), so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider and the dispute remains under POL-NS-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-CHAT-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver sent two chat messages (06:42:30 and 06:46:02, both delivered and read) and placed an in-app voice call at 06:45:10 that the rider did not answer. Even if the rider had sent a message, the unanswered call recorded in trip_record.in_app_calls means POL-NS-04(b) would not be satisfied; in fact the rider sent nothing, so the clause cannot apply.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "At the 06:41:20 arrival marker the driver was 14.47 m from the pin and stationary in the dwell run (0.0 kph), not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 kph or above, so the arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05. The recomputed dwell from the first qualifying fix is 507 seconds, which meets the 300-second minimum, so under POL-NS-05(iii) the fee is not defeated.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The effective in-geofence dwell is 507 seconds, far longer than the 300-second STANDARD minimum, so there is no waiting-period shortfall under POL-NS-06. The traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no advisory covers Woodlands Ave 6 and POL-NS-06(i) cannot be used to accumulate intervals; but the driver's dwell was a single continuous 507-second run with no exit from the geofence, so no accumulation is needed and the fee is not refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-ADVIS-00207-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 equals the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) under the fee_schedule resolution rule, and matches fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee. The fee is therefore properly chargeable under POL-NS-01 and there is no fare defect under POL-NS-08(d).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede that the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check trips on the driver's own profile: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (at least 4) and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d (61) is 11.5%, greater than 0.08, so both limbs are met. Compensation of SGD 3.20 is therefore withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d); the escalation packet must direct the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full, and the fee is held meanwhile rather than collected or refunded by the automated pipeline. This is a platform guard on the driver's termination volume, not a finding that the rider was present or that the fee was wrongly charged; the rider's own counters do not trigger escalation (rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, not 3 or more, and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both sides).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207", "EV-RPROF-00207", "EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare breakdown shows payment_status PENDING and refund_issued_sgd 0.0, so the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is held and has not been refunded to the rider. Under POL-NS-09 escalation is terminal: the Judge issues no monetary ruling and the disputed fee is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded while human review is pending, so the rider's request for a refund is not granted in the automated ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim that he came down is contradicted by his device being 1.9 km away with zero qualifying presence fixes, while the trip record shows the driver waited 8.3 minutes (wait_time_min) and held a 507-second in-geofence dwell before cancelling. On the merits the rider's claim is unsupported and the no-show fee stands under POL-NS-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record contains a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-07-29T06:41:20+08:00, satisfying POL-NS-01(a), and the GPS trace places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at or before that event: derived.arrival shows 52 qualifying fixes, with the longest continuous qualifying run beginning at 06:41:10 (before the arrived event) and lasting 507 seconds, and derived.driver_track.min_distance_m is 14.47 m. This meets POL-NS-02's test of at least 3 consecutive in-radius fixes with 25 m or better accuracy, so POL-NS-01(b) is satisfied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00207", "EV-GPS-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The continuous in-geofence dwell measured from the first qualifying fix is 507 seconds (derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec), which exceeds the fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec of 300 seconds for a STANDARD zone class under POL-NS-01(c). The driver therefore held position well past the required five-minute dwell; the trip record's wait_time_min of 8.3 and time_to_arrival_min of 8.5 corroborate the wait.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record shows no boarding event (started_at and ended_at are null) and that the trip was terminated by the driver at 2026-07-29T06:49:37+08:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three reason codes recognised by POL-NS-01(d). The 300-second dwell elapsed at 06:46:10, so the cancellation was at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed. DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is not the code, so POL-NS-01(d) is satisfied and POL-NS-03 does not redirect the case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in fare_breakdown equals the amount produced by fee_schedule.resolution_rule: the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is SGD 4.00. The contested amount is the cancellation-fee line, not the separate SGD 0.50 platform fee, and the cancellation-fee line reconciles, so there is no fare defect under POL-NS-08(d) and the fee is the amount fixed by POL-NS-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim that he came down is contradicted by the GPS rider track: derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0 and derived.rider_presence shows the rider's device was about 1.9 km away for the whole window (max_distance_m 1906.56 m, mean_distance_m 1900.40 m), far outside the 100 m STANDARD rider presence radius, so limb (c) of POL-NS-04 is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes. The chat log also shows the rider sent no message at all (only system and driver messages appear), so POL-NS-04(a) fails and the rider is not exonerated; the driver's message 'boss im downstairs at 682' at 06:42:30 and the unanswered in-app call placed at 06:45:10 (recorded in trip_record.in_app_calls) show the driver was at the pickup and trying to coordinate.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-CHAT-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05 does not apply: at the arrived_at timestamp of 06:41:20 the driver was already inside the 50 m geofence (the qualifying run began at 06:41:10) and stationary, not more than 300 m from the pin and not travelling at 15 km/h or above (derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph includes 0.0 and the dwell run shows a stationary hold). The arrival marker is therefore not false, and even if recomputed the corrected dwell of 507 seconds meets the minimum under POL-NS-05(iii), so the fee is not defeated.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00207", "EV-GPS-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06 does not apply because the effective in-geofence dwell is 507 seconds, longer than the 300-second STANDARD minimum, so there is no waiting-period shortfall. I cite EV-ADVIS-00207-01, which is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), only for its absence: no traffic advisory covers Woodlands Ave 6 in this window, so no KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT advisory can be used to accumulate separate intervals or reduce the minimum under POL-NS-06(i); none is needed because the continuous dwell already exceeds the minimum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-ADVIS-00207-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede that the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is met on the driver profile: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more) and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d (61) is approximately 0.115, which is greater than 0.08. Both limbs are satisfied, so under POL-NS-07 driver compensation is WITHHELD and the case must escalate under POL-NS-09; the driver cannot receive DRIVER_COMPENSATION in this automated ruling. No other profile field is used for this check, and driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags (0) is a lifetime counter and is not the trailing-30-day figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only escalation trigger present is POL-NS-09(d) via the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check. The rider-side limb of POL-NS-09(d) is not met: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the threshold of 3 (rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and is not this field). POL-NS-09(c) is not met: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, together fewer than 2. Therefore escalation is required, and under POL-GEN-03 and POL-NS-09 the disputed fee is held rather than collected or refunded: fare_breakdown.payment_status is PENDING and refund_issued_sgd is 0.0. The escalation packet must record the POL-NS-07 instruction to the reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207", "EV-RPROF-00207", "EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the merits of this trip, the rider's refund claim is unsupported: all four limbs of POL-NS-01 are satisfied, no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and the rider was about 1.9 km away with zero qualifying presence fixes while the driver waited 507 seconds and announced his location. The rider's own filed statement that he 'came down' is contradicted by the rider track and by his silence in the chat log. The fee is legitimately chargeable to the rider; it is only withheld from the driver and escalated because of the separate anti-farming pattern, not because the rider's claim has merit.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207", "EV-CHAT-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207", "EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
